From 5cd9f5d072732dfba881ae6e7527ce8aecebd6b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 21:14:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] settings: a setting for the two views of 3D Blu-ray video

"Decode both views of 3D Blu-ray video (MVC)" (videoplayer.hades3dmvc),
with the stereoscopic settings of the video player, on by default.

With it, a video that codes the picture of each eye as a view of its
own (H.264 MVC) has both views decoded, by the processor, and is shown
as a stereoscopic video. Without it such a video plays in 2D as it
always did, with hardware decoding.

The strings are English in the core file (39960, 39961) and are
translated in Estuary (31721, 31722: English, and Spanish in its three
variants), as the other settings of Hades.

Nothing reads the setting yet.

Read and compiled (the settings dialog); not seen in the settings.
---
