+#. Hades: label of setting "videoplayer.hades3dmvc"; translated in Estuary (#31721)
+#: system/settings/settings.xml
+msgctxt "#39960"
+msgid "Decode both views of 3D Blu-ray video (MVC)"
+msgstr ""
+
+#. Hades: help of setting "videoplayer.hades3dmvc"; translated in Estuary (#31722)
+#: system/settings/settings.xml
+msgctxt "#39961"
+msgid "A 3D Blu-ray holds the picture of each eye as a view of its own (H.264 MVC), and so does a Matroska file made of one. With this setting both views are decoded, by the processor, and the video is shown as a stereoscopic one. Without it, or where the second view cannot be decoded, the video plays in 2D as before, with hardware decoding. Applies from the next video."
+msgstr ""
+
+#empty strings from id 39962 to 39979
 
